<%!-- The username page: everything about your profile address in one place.
Three cards, in the order the questions come up — what is my address (and how
do I copy it), how do I change it, and what do I use for a link that has to keep
working forever.

It used to be a bare rename form buried under Sign-in & security, where nobody
looks for a handle, while the permanent link sat on that same security page
reading like a credential. Both are public identity, so both live here under
Profile now. --%>
<.settings_shell user={@user} active={:username} title={gettext("Username")}>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <%!-- What your address is right now. The Copy buttons are a progressive
    enhancement (data-copy, app.js); without JS the select-all <code> still lets
    you copy it by hand. --%>
    <.card>
      <.section_title>{gettext("Your profile address")}</.section_title>
      <.copy_field id="profile-url">{url(~p"/#{@user}")}</.copy_field>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {gettext("Other members mention you as %{handle}.", handle: "@#{@user.username}")}
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card>
      <.section_title>{gettext("Change your username")}</.section_title>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {gettext(
          "Changing it automatically rewrites every mention of your old handle in posts to the new one and notifies those posts' authors. Your old profile address stops working."
        )}
      </p>

      <%!-- How many posts will be rewritten, so the member knows the blast
      radius before renaming. --%>
      <p :if={@mention_count > 0} class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <%= ngettext(
          "%{formatted} post currently mentions %{handle} and will be updated when you rename.",
          "%{formatted} posts currently mention %{handle} and will be updated when you rename.",
          @mention_count,
          formatted: compact_count(@mention_count),
          handle: "@#{@user.username}"
        ) %>
      </p>

      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <%= gettext("You can change your username up to %{limit} times within %{days} days.",
          limit: @quota.limit,
          days: @quota.window_days
        ) %>
        <%= if @quota.remaining > 0 do %>
          <%= gettext("%{remaining} of %{limit} changes left.",
            remaining: @quota.remaining,
            limit: @quota.limit
          ) %>
        <% end %>
      </p>

      <%= if @quota.remaining > 0 do %>
        <div class="mt-4">
          <%= render("form_content.html",
            backlink: ~p"/settings",
            changeset: @changeset,
            action: ~p"/settings/username",
            user: @user
          ) %>
        </div>
      <% else %>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          <%= gettext("You have used all %{limit} username changes of the last %{days} days.",
            limit: @quota.limit,
            days: @quota.window_days
          ) %>
          <%= gettext("You can change it again on %{date}.",
            date: Calendar.strftime(@quota.next_change_at, "%Y-%m-%d")
          ) %>
        </p>
      <% end %>
    </.card>

    <%!-- Permanent profile link (issue #904): a username-independent URL that
    redirects to this member's current profile, so a link built from it survives
    a future rename. Read-only, nothing to configure. It belongs right under the
    rename form: this is the answer to "but then my old links break". --%>
    <.card>
      <.section_title>{gettext("Permanent profile link")}</.section_title>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {gettext(
          "This link always opens your profile, even after you change your username. It is built from a fixed id, so it never breaks on a rename. For everyday sharing the short address above is friendlier."
        )}
      </p>
      <.copy_field id="permalink-url" code_class="text-xs">
        {url(~p"/system/permalinks/users/#{@user.id}")}
      </.copy_field>
    </.card>
  </div>
</.settings_shell>
